WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back!
-Thank you! Wow!

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.469 line:92%
-It's lovely to have you back.

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:04.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
You and Rosie are friends.
You know each other.

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:05.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, we are.
-We are friends.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were on the ill-fated --
I don't know --

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.109 line:92%
season whatever of "The View."

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Donald Trump is
our through line.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.880
So, he came out, and she was
supposed to fight with me.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.281 line:92%
And she said, "He's a racist."

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.616 line:92%
And I was like, "Mm-hmm."

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:19.552
And then she -- "He's terrible."
I was like, "Mm-hmm."

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that was it.
We both got fired.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:24.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right?
-Yes, pretty much.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:25.859 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I want to ask about --

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:27.961 size:88% position:44%
There's so many things
I want to ask you about.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:28.628 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But the shutdown --

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
it seems like everyone is in
agreement, pretty much.

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:33.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's maybe some
far-right holdouts

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.234 line:92%
that Trump won this game.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
But everybody seems to agree
that Nancy Pelosi

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:37.137 size:81% position:41% line:92%
played this perfectly.

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:40.607
What do you think is the fallout
from this for the president?

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:42.609 size:88% position:44%
-Well, the fallout is --
those far-right holdouts

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:44.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
are calling us, you know,
from blocked numbers,

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:46.046 size:88% position:44% line:92%
saying, "Yeah, he lost."

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.348
I mean, the holdout is --
even the wackiest part

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:51.885
of his base thinks he's a giant
loser for this whole caper.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
No, seriously.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:58.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's not because
they disagree about the wall.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:01.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
They just think that,
strategically, he failed.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.363 line:92%
They think that he was owned

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:06.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
publicly and privately
by Nancy Pelosi.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's sort of an
insider point,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it was his
son-in-law, Jared Kushner,

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:10.470 size:81% position:41% line:92%
who ran point on this.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they think he's not
up for the task

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:14.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
of running legislative affairs
for The White House.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:17.911
-She seemed, at every level, to
know exactly what to do.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was the taking away of the
State of the Union --

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:22.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was taking away something
that ceremonial

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:26.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the president
a stroke of genius from Nancy?

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:30.356
-It's a mistake to project onto
him more sophistication

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:36.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
than exists, and for him,
taking away air time,

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:39.632 size:78% position:39%
taking away the thing
that we all recognize

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the movies and whatnot
about being president,

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
standing there with
the people behind you

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
clapping or booing
or whatever they're doing.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:48.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
That, to him --
Those are some of the most

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:51.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of powerful
and precious things to him

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.378 size:81% position:41% line:92%
about being president.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.613 size:75% position:38% line:92%
So to take that away

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:56.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
really did sort of
cut all of his leverage.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, of course,
it's happening on the same day

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:01.421
that he capitulates there,
Roger Stone is indicted.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:04.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
You traveled in
Republican circles

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:06.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he was in those circles,
as well, Roger Stone.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was your take on
Roger Stone?

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:11.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, he was at a firm
that was so dirty,

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:14.801
you just knew that if no one
else would hire a bad dictator,

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, "Oh, well,
that firm will do it."

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.071 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It was Stone, Manafort,

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:20.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's awaiting sentencing
for his felonies.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:25.011
And, you know, the idea that
we're all supposed to believe --

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
Chris Christie
was on my show today,

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:28.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I said, "You know,
everyone around the president

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:32.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
has either been convicted
or is awaiting trial

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the crime of
lying about Russia.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.455 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Is that a coincidence?"

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:36.523 line:92%
"Eh, it might be a coincidence."

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:38.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, everyone that
the president

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:39.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
surrounded himself with
is either

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.428
a convicted felon or
has been charged with a felony.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:46.299
-You talked to Chris Christie
today, and it was a very long --

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
You talked to him
for about 40 minutes,

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was
a fascinating interview.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:50.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't think it
was that long, was it?

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:51.738 line:92%
-No, I was -- But, again,

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:54.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wanted to hear you
interview him.

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:55.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
he wrote this book,

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it seems to be a thing
that a lot of people

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.779
leave the Trump administration,
and then they take this

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:03.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
one shot at sort of
reframing their experience,

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:06.219 size:75% position:38%
because they are now
trying to, you know,

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.121 size:88% position:44% line:92%
re-enter polite society.

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:12.392
Do you think Chris Christie will
be effective with this book,

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
with his take on
what had happened

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:14.661 size:88% position:44% line:92%
inside that White House?

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.863 size:84% position:42%
-I think Chris Christie
is like Donald Trump,

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
in that people know
what they think about him.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if you're from
New Jersey, you know,

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:23.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
he left with some of
the lowest approval ratings

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.004 size:88% position:44% line:92%
in that state's history.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:27.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think if you're in
the Republican Party

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you see a lot of people
were into Trump,

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:33.546
Chris Christie has some of that
bluntness without, you know,

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:36.983
all of the criminality that
seems to follow Donald Trump.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:39.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I do think
something that's similar

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:40.587 line:92%
with the two of them is they --

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:43.056 size:84% position:42%
The people were charmed
by their authenticity.

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:45.291 size:78% position:39%
You know, and, again,
it was no small thing

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Chris Christie
was, you know,

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:48.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
a Republican governor
in New Jersey.

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:52.465
-Yeah. And, look, Chris Christie
has genuine friendships

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:53.733 line:92%
on the other side of the aisle.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't want to
name any of them.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:57.170
They may be in witness
protection at this point.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:57.870 size:81% position:41% line:92%
But, I mean, he did --

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.406
-"I got the kind of friends that
don't like the world knowing."

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:04.344
-No, no. But he -- And has
obvious political talents.

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:06.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
The challenge I think
he'll have with the book is --

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:10.283
he savages Jared Kushner,
the president's son-in-law.

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:13.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
He spares nothing.
And Kushner deserves it.

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:17.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
Savages Bannon.
Bannon deserves it.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said this to him on TV,
so don't feel like

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:21.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm talking about him behind
his back on TV.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:25.131
But he doesn't lay a glove,
really, on the president.

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:26.599 line:92%
And the president puts those

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:29.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
incompetent and
seemingly corrupt people

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:29.736 size:88% position:44% line:92%
in very powerful places.

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.871 size:78% position:39%
-Yeah, I guess that's
the disconnect is --

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:33.406 size:88% position:44%
how can you say it's not
the president's fault?

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:36.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's surrounded by, you know,
sort of liars and idiots,

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:39.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
because that seems to be,
like, a pretty important part

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:42.649
of the job is who you bring into
The White House with you.

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:46.185
-The president has surrou--
There weren't any qualifications

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
to work on the Trump campaign
or you didn't really

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:50.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
have to know how to do
anything political.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:50.890 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you had to know Russians,
like Russians,

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then lie about
what you did with them.

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:59.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
That's a weird thing to have.

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:05.238
That's -- You had that in
"special skills" on the résumé.

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:07.540 line:92%
-Maybe it was, like -- Yeah...

